{"name":"Cedar Ridge","hex":"#9b6663","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cedar Ridge","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A census-designated place in Tuolumne County, California, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cedar_Ridge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cedar Ridge, Nevada County, California","blocks":[{"text":"Cedar Ridge is an unincorporated community in Nevada County, California, United States, along State Route 174 2.5 miles (4.0 km) east/southeast of Grass Valley, California. and approximately 1 mile (1.6 km) east/southeast of the Empire Mine in Gold Country."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Cedar_Ridge_post_office.jpg/330px-Cedar_Ridge_post_office.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedar_Ridge%2C_Nevada_County%2C_California","wikidata":"Q5056862"},{"title":"Cedar Ridge, Tuolumne County, California","blocks":[{"text":"Cedar Ridge is a census-designated place (CDP) in Tuolumne County, California, United States. Cedar Ridge sits at an elevation of 3,760 feet (1,150 m). The 2020 United States census reported Cedar Ridge's population as 1,235."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedar_Ridge%2C_Tuolumne_County%2C_California","wikidata":"Q5056864"},{"title":"Cedar Ridge (Disputanta, Virginia)","blocks":[{"text":"Cedar Ridge is a historic home located East of Disputanta, in Surry County, Virginia. The original one-room section was built about 1750, and later enlarged to a 1+1⁄2-story, three-bay, single pile, Colonial frame dwelling. The main house has a later rear addition of an enclosed breezeway connecting to a two-story kitchen and bedchamber addition. The footprint of the house resembles a modified \"T\" shape. The house was restored, and the chimneys rebuilt, in the late-1970s. Also on the property is a one-story outbuilding that may once have served as slaves' quarters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Gate_at_the_entrance_to_Cedar_Ridge%2C_night.jpg/330px-Gate_at_the_entrance_to_Cedar_Ridge%2C_night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedar_Ridge_(Disputanta%2C_Virginia)","wikidata":"Q15208223"},{"title":"Ridge","blocks":[{"text":"A ridge is a long, narrow, elevated geomorphologic landform, structural feature, or a combination of both separated from the surrounding terrain by steep sides. The sides of a ridge slope away from a narrow top, the crest or ridgecrest, with the terrain dropping down on either side. The crest, if narrow, is also called a ridgeline. Limitations on the dimensions of a ridge are lacking. Its height above the surrounding terrain can vary from less than a meter to hundreds of meters. A ridge can be either depositional, erosional, tectonic, or a combination of these in origin and can consist of either bedrock, loose sediment, lava, or ice depending on its origin. A ridge can occur as either an isolated, independent feature or part of a larger geomorphological and/or structural feature. Frequently, a ridge can be further subdivided into smaller geomorphic or structural elements."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/%E4%B8%AD%E6%A9%AB%E5%85%AC%E8%B7%AF%E7%9C%BA%E6%9C%9B%E6%A2%A8%E5%B1%B1%E5%8F%8A%E9%9B%AA%E5%B1%B1%E5%8D%97%E7%A8%9C2.jpg/330px-%E4%B8%AD%E6%A9%AB%E5%85%AC%E8%B7%AF%E7%9C%BA%E6%9C%9B%E6%A2%A8%E5%B1%B1%E5%8F%8A%E9%9B%AA%E5%B1%B1%E5%8D%97%E7%A8%9C2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ridge","wikidata":"Q740445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Cedar_Ridge_country_store.jpg/500px-Cedar_Ridge_country_store.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Cedar_Ridge_country_store.jpg/1280px-Cedar_Ridge_country_store.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Cedar_Ridge_country_store.jpg/500px-Cedar_Ridge_country_store.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cedar Ridge country store","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACedar_Ridge_country_store.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Tsubakurodake_from_Otenshodake_2002-8-22.jpg/500px-Tsubakurodake_from_Otenshodake_2002-8-22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Tsubakurodake_from_Otenshodake_2002-8-22.jpg/500px-Tsubakurodake_from_Otenshodake_2002-8-22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A mountain ridge from Mount Otensho to Mount Tsubakuro in Japan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATsubakurodake_from_Otenshodake_2002-8-22.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/The_Table1.jpg/500px-The_Table1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/The_Table1.jpg/1280px-The_Table1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/The_Table1.jpg/500px-The_Table1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The edges of tuyas can form ridges.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Table1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Vihren_Pirin_IMG_0859.jpg/500px-Vihren_Pirin_IMG_0859.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Vihren_Pirin_IMG_0859.jpg/1280px-Vihren_Pirin_IMG_085